# Exsecutor source holds itself to §8.1: UTF-8, no BOM, LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# --- vendor/: third-party, byte-exact, DO NOT NORMALISE ---
#
# vendor/fasmg-x86/ is upstream fasmg's x86 macro package, vendored verbatim.
# Upstream ships CRLF; 71 of its 72 files contain CR. That is a deliberate
# exception to the LF rule above, not an oversight.
#
# The whole reason vendoring is defensible is that the tree is byte-identical
# to upstream and provable by hash (see vendor/fasmg-x86/PROVENANCE.md). If git
# normalised these line endings on checkout -- which it would on any clone with
# core.autocrlf=true -- the recorded digest would no longer reproduce and the
# re-vendor diff would show every file as changed. `-text` disables all EOL
# conversion in both directions.
vendor/fasmg-x86/** -text

# PROVENANCE.md is ours, not upstream's, and is excluded from the digest.
vendor/fasmg-x86/PROVENANCE.md text eol=lf
